00:25:29.069 --> 00:25:31.150
And Kenneth, playing Josh, I'm sure you get this question.
肯尼斯（Kenneth）扮演乔什（Josh），我相信你会明白这个问题。

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:33.710
A lot of Kenneth, playing says, hey Josh, can you give me some advice?
很多肯尼思在打球时都会说，嘿乔什，你能给我一些建议吗？

00:25:33.710 --> 00:25:38.349
Is someone who wants to be an actor or share a story of how you became such a great actor?
有人想成为一名演员或分享你如何成为一名如此出色的演员的故事吗？

00:25:41.509 --> 00:25:44.450
Well, I trained a really long time.
嗯，我训练了很长时间。

00:25:44.450 --> 00:25:48.789
I did a lot of plays.
我演过很多戏。

00:25:48.789 --> 00:25:59.269
I went to a lot of theaters and apprenticed and interned and did non-equity companies, and then I went to grad school and worked around the clock for three straight years.
我去了很多剧院，当过学徒，实习过，还做过非股权公司，然后我读了研究生，连续三年昼夜不停地工作。

00:26:00.470 --> 00:26:01.349
And then I got out of school.
然后我就离开了学校。

00:26:01.349 --> 00:26:05.190
I was very fortunate to get signed by a really great agent.
我很幸运能得到一位非常出色的经纪人的签约。

00:26:05.190 --> 00:26:08.950
And I just started working.
而我刚刚开始工作。

00:26:09.890 --> 00:26:17.450
The thing is though, like when I got out of schools, 1999, it was a different world of entertainment.
但问题是，就像 1999 年我离开学校时一样，那是一个不同的娱乐世界。

00:26:17.450 --> 00:26:19.690
It was a different, I mean, everything was different.
这是不同的，我的意思是，一切都不同了。

00:26:19.690 --> 00:26:28.170
So I think the, you know, there's people who are all, you know, a lot of people are like, the good old days were, blah, blah, blah.
所以我认为，你知道，很多人都喜欢，过去的美好时光是，等等，等等。

00:26:28.170 --> 00:26:45.769
And I'm not really one for that kind of nostalgia, but I do think that right now, I don't know that you, you know, if school is your thing, if that's where you thrive, it can be great to go to school and study a craft and be with a company of people that you're learning with.
我并不是那种怀旧的人，但我确实认为，现在，我不知道你，你知道，如果学校是你的事，如果那是你成长的地方，那么去学校学习一门手艺并与一群与你一起学习的人在一起会很棒。

00:26:45.769 --> 00:26:56.690
But if you don't have the time, or the wherewithal, or the money to do that, take your phone and start making cool stuff.
但如果你没有时间、资金或金钱来做到这一点，那就拿起你的手机开始制作很酷的东西。

00:26:56.690 --> 00:27:01.970
Make cool movies, learn how to edit, learn how to be indispensable.
制作很酷的电影，学习如何剪辑，学习如何变得不可或缺。

00:27:04.250 --> 00:27:07.089
You're not gonna be as good as you wanna be.
你不会像你想的那样优秀。

00:27:07.089 --> 00:27:14.490
Ira Glass has that great quote about how when you're younger, your taste is much better than your abilities, so it's really hard.
艾拉·格拉斯（Ira Glass）有句名言，说当你年轻的时候，你的品味比你的能力要好得多，所以这真的很难。

00:27:14.490 --> 00:27:22.369
and you have to work until your art catches up with your taste, which is probably pretty good, even young.
你必须努力工作，直到你的艺术赶上你的品味，这可能相当不错，即使是年轻的。

00:27:22.369 --> 00:27:37.769
So you just gotta get a lot of hours under your belt and work with good people and humble yourself and ask questions and be curious and stay not cynical somehow, you know, because the business is really hard and can beat you up and spit you out.
所以你必须花很多时间和优秀的人一起工作，谦虚自己，提出问题，保持好奇心，不要愤世嫉俗，你知道，因为这个行业真的很难，可能会打败你，然后把你吐出来。

00:27:37.769 --> 00:27:47.410
But you just gotta stick with good people and ask the right questions and just be in the right place at the right time, and by that, I mean, just keep going.
但你只需要和优秀的人在一起，提出正确的问题，在正确的时间出现在正确的地点，我的意思是，继续前进。

00:27:47.410 --> 00:27:49.990
Yeah.
是的。

00:27:49.990 --> 00:28:02.640
Craig, Brendan Yuri-Lover says, I want to know more about your writing career, any future books, you just finished this one, any future books, big fan of the book you wrote, and I want to be an author like you.
克雷格，布伦丹·尤里·洛弗说，我想更多地了解你的写作生涯，任何未来的书，你刚刚完成了这本书，任何未来的书，你写的书的忠实粉丝，我想成为像你一样的作家。

